	In the days before BootX, it was sometimes useful to boot from
OF using a floppy disk containing vmlinux.coff (which is what "make
zImage" builds):

-rwxr-xr-x   1 root     root       998439 Jun 21 14:36 arch/ppc/coffboot/vmlinux.coff
-rwxr-xr-x   1 root     root      2889970 Jun 21 14:36 vmlinux

> file arch/ppc/coffboot/vmlinux.coff
arch/ppc/coffboot/vmlinux.coff: executable (RISC System/6000 V3.1) or obj module not stripped

I suppose it's still useful in case the MacOS partition gets hosed,
although I haven't tried it in a while.

